      "content": "gobbling up? lol that's a weird way to put it. i guess i see the pun with \"gobbling\" and \"goblin\" but it's a bit of a stretch for a business report. \n\nso if the value is being \"gobbled up\" every year, does that mean the asset is basically getting eaten away by usage? and are there other things that act like those \"goblins\" to speed up the loss of value, like unexpected stuff happening in the warehouse?",
